openvino_bevfusion: reuse the sparse encoder's output-cell table.

For each strided convolution the sparse encoder finds the output voxels on
the CPU with a dense table of every output cell. The table was allocated and
filled with -1 on every inference: 720x720x21 ints (44 MB) at the first
strided level, about 50 MB in total. That took about 20 ms per inference,
half of the encoder's time, for tables in which only a few tens of thousands
of cells are ever set.

Keep one table per strided level across inferences and reset only the cells
the inference set. The output voxels and their order are unchanged, so the
results are identical. On an Intel Arc Pro B60 the encoder takes about 25 ms
instead of 44 ms.

Remove this patch once openvino_contrib carries an equivalent change.

